grid: the Grid command line

Usage: grid <command> [flags]

Commands:
  version     print the CLI, contract and app_min versions
  where       show which project and task a folder belongs to
  doctor      check machine health and collect a support bundle
  hook        answer a Claude Code or Codex hook event; set and list hook levels
  task        new, show, list, status, stop, close, reopen, history, attach, move
  plan        write, check, items, hash, diff, migrate
  views       render the task pages (not built yet)
  job         next, post, ack, result, cancel, tree, blocked, render, lint, show, verify, cycles, floor
  lease       take, renew, release, status (merge or task lease)
  feed        tick, post, read, state, types, handover, fold
  mcp         stdio server with the Feed tools
  question    add, withdraw, list, tick and sync task questions
  ask         ask a person a question (not built yet)
  answer      record a person's answer
  approve     approve a gate (a person or the app only)
  refusal     decide a refused command (a person or the app only)
  decide      alias for refusal decide
  deliver     write the outcome and raise the ship gate
  proof       add evidence and rebuild the task proof index
  history     append a dated task history line
  land        land a task per the deploy topic
  brain       show, search, topics, index, propose, accept, keep, decide
  machine     machines topic (not built yet)
  env         up, down browser Job dev environments
  ports       claim, release, list, gc dev port blocks
  deploy      deploy topic (not built yet)
  person      check person access; list, show and find approvers
  routine     add, list, remove, run, schedule and unschedule routines
  worker      list local grid-worker processes
  agent       check agent readiness; set models and efforts; list settings
  workflow    show workflow template files and parse problems
  skill       enable, disable and list skills
  session     list, show, start, stop, send, pause, resume, handback, switch
  intent      list, claim, done (worker requests)
  usage       post and show usage, set budgets and notice thresholds, fold observed session totals
  account     agent accounts (not built yet)
  project     add, remove, list, scan and relink projects
  project-md  get or set a project front-matter key
  setup       record validated project setup answers
  signal      add, act on and dismiss inbox signals
  artifact    import, link, list and publish task artifacts
  eval        list, run and show task evaluations
  migrate     upgrade the Grid home to this format
  sync        sync with a Grid server (not built yet)

Exit status: 0 done, 1 failed, 2 usage, 3 rejected (stale lease, invalid record or intent claim token; do not retry), 4 disk full, 5 taken (intent already claimed or done; skip).
